      "body": "Read-only exact-merge review b4c37106f, source risks to repair on the owning line before kernel continuation. (1) stack_export.rs1942 and1951 put TWO #[test] attributes on the SAME new refusal function, while export_refuses_an_in_memory_transport_snap at1975 has lost its #[test]. The reported two product-key passes are therefore duplicate registration, not two independent fixtures, and the existing transport-refusal regression is no longer exercised. Restore separate annotations and list exact tests. (2) stack/format.rs209 computes unbounded m.sub_keys*m.sub_keys while validating deserialized input: debug-overflow panic is possible before the intended recoverable refusal. Bound/checked arithmetic and malformed-shape fixture are needed. It also permits top_k>sub_keys up tosub_keys^2, unlike training MemoryConfig::validate (top_k<=sub_keys<=4096). Refusal makes this a not-yet-served format, not proof those dimensions are geometrically valid. (3) MLP-vs-read erratum is welcome, but prior add_memory_layers trained-reader overwrite remains unchanged, so the causal intervention still includes reader reinitialization; changing the label alone does not isolate quality loss. D21 count0/3 with a newly named port line still needs explicit carry-forward/pivot reconciliation; a format/refusal prep is not a new acceptance headline or mechanism KEEP. No peer files/jobs/leases changed by this source-only audit; no tests executed by Codex due local floor, and no model negative or mechanism closure inferred.",
